WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:49.884
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:50.154 --> 00:53.324
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

3
01:00.206 --> 01:04.585
EPISODE 8: A WORLD BUILT ON HYPOCRISY

4
01:14.970 --> 01:17.014
That'll be 28,300 won.

5
01:17.723 --> 01:18.974
- Here you go. - Thank you.

6
01:21.143 --> 01:22.645
- You're all set. - Thank you.

7
01:22.728 --> 01:24.355
Have a nice day.

8
01:55.302 --> 01:58.806
BROTHER-IN-LAW DID YOU EAT LUNCH YET?

9
02:00.766 --> 02:03.477
Why here? We could've eaten something better.

10
02:03.561 --> 02:05.813
If you come to Busan, a pork gukbap is a must.

11
02:06.272 --> 02:08.441
Actually, I was craving it.

12
02:08.524 --> 02:09.817
I get to eat it, thanks to you.

13
02:09.900 --> 02:10.901
Eat up.

14
02:10.985 --> 02:12.737
You too.

15
02:19.118 --> 02:21.162
What is this?

16
02:21.829 --> 02:23.581
A-yeong's tutoring is expensive.

17
02:23.664 --> 02:24.957
I wanted to help out.

18
02:26.250 --> 02:28.461
It costs more to live in Seoul.

19
02:28.919 --> 02:32.798
We don't have to pay rent, and we both work

20
02:32.882 --> 02:35.551
- so we're all right. - A-yeong is my niece.

21
02:35.634 --> 02:36.927
I want to do this.

22
02:38.262 --> 02:39.764
Then we'll put it to good use.

23
02:40.473 --> 02:42.057
Thank you as always, Eun-tae.

24
02:42.141 --> 02:43.434
It's nothing.

25
02:48.022 --> 02:49.648
How is my brother doing lately?

26
02:49.732 --> 02:51.609
Well...

27
02:52.026 --> 02:53.736
I'm sure he's doing fine.

28
02:55.654 --> 02:58.115
He works nights, so we rarely see each other.

29
02:59.241 --> 03:01.786
Well, I feel bad for him.

30
03:02.328 --> 03:05.623
He used to be so successful, but now he seems so dejected.

31
03:06.248 --> 03:08.292
Back in the day

32
03:08.375 --> 03:12.087
Gong Eun-seok was synonymous with Busan's fashion scene.

33
03:12.838 --> 03:17.092
He was the first person to bring items trending in Japan

34
03:17.176 --> 03:18.969
to the Busan market.

35
03:19.053 --> 03:22.264
Those shabby-looking clothes sold so well.

36
03:22.348 --> 03:23.891
Yes, I remember now.

37
03:24.350 --> 03:26.268
The neighborhood went crazy back then.

38
03:26.977 --> 03:28.562
After he became successful

39
03:29.021 --> 03:31.941
he bought me Korean beef to celebrate my college admission.

40
03:32.733 --> 03:34.819
That was my first time having Korean beef.

41
03:34.902 --> 03:37.154
I had no clue it was that good. It was delicious.

42
03:37.530 --> 03:39.365
Thanks to Eun-seok

43
03:39.448 --> 03:42.743
I still have a habit of eating that whenever something good happens.

44
03:43.452 --> 03:45.538
Was it the barbecue place in Seomyeon?

45
03:46.580 --> 03:48.249
Yes, have you ever been?

46
03:48.332 --> 03:50.501
That's where he seduced me.

47
03:50.584 --> 03:53.212
So the mere mention of Korean beef makes me shudder.

48
03:59.093 --> 04:00.261
Actually...

49
04:01.887 --> 04:04.431
Eun-seok asked me for money yesterday.

50
04:04.932 --> 04:05.933
Again?

51
04:06.851 --> 04:09.144
I'm so sorry, Eun-tae.

52
04:09.645 --> 04:12.106
What will I do with that man?

53
04:13.107 --> 04:15.484
That's not why I'm bringing it up.

54
04:17.027 --> 04:19.613
He said he wanted to start a business

55
04:20.322 --> 04:22.199
but I told him I couldn't give him the money.

56
04:23.075 --> 04:25.703
In my opinion, I don't think it'll do well.

57
04:26.620 --> 04:30.165
But I could be wrong.

58
04:30.875 --> 04:32.668
His business might end up doing well.

59
04:33.419 --> 04:36.922
So in the hope that I'm wrong

60
04:37.882 --> 04:40.509
I want to help him out how I can.

61
04:41.719 --> 04:42.970
With that being said

62
04:43.304 --> 04:45.681
I hope you can accept this money.

63
04:50.853 --> 04:52.396
Don't hate my brother too much.

64
04:54.148 --> 04:56.150
He may seem a bit lousy right now

65
04:57.401 --> 04:58.527
but I still think

66
04:59.820 --> 05:01.947
he's a great person.

67
05:04.408 --> 05:05.409
Gosh.

68
05:05.993 --> 05:07.411
He's a lucky man.

69
05:08.078 --> 05:11.999
Even in his lousy state, his brother thinks he's great.

70
05:12.082 --> 05:15.294
At one time, he was the coolest person I knew.

71
05:16.337 --> 05:18.422
But right now, I think you're the coolest.

72
05:19.048 --> 05:21.342
Me? Why is that?

73
05:21.425 --> 05:23.218
You haven't given up on him.

74
05:24.219 --> 05:25.930
Gosh, what are you saying?

75
05:26.639 --> 05:28.182
Hurry up and eat.

76
06:03.425 --> 06:05.427
INCOMING CALL TEAM 4 MR. JEONG SEON-HYUK

77
06:09.223 --> 06:10.224
Thank you.

78
06:13.477 --> 06:14.770
How's work these days?

79
06:16.647 --> 06:18.399
You know how it goes.

80
06:19.191 --> 06:20.401
It's always the same.

81
06:21.860 --> 06:23.779
Sure, work is all the same.

82
06:24.905 --> 06:27.533
So how long will you stay at Hongsung?

83
06:31.453 --> 06:33.122
I haven't thought about it.

84
06:34.081 --> 06:35.582
How about some food for thought?

85
06:36.250 --> 06:38.460
I believe I already rejected your offer.

86
06:39.294 --> 06:40.921
Our company merged.

87
06:41.005 --> 06:42.131
I'm no longer the CEO.

88
06:43.507 --> 06:44.800
Does that mean

89
06:45.509 --> 06:47.177
you've joined a bigger company?

90
06:52.391 --> 06:53.767
An article will come out tomorrow.

91
06:54.685 --> 06:56.437
It'll send quite a shock through the market.

92
07:02.401 --> 07:04.028
Korea Branch Manager of CGM?

93
07:04.987 --> 07:06.697
CGM is entering the Korean market.

94
07:07.489 --> 07:09.366
Based on our predictions

95
07:09.450 --> 07:12.578
all small and medium-sized brand controllers in Korea will disappear.

96
07:12.661 --> 07:13.704
It looks like

97
07:13.787 --> 07:16.081
Hongsung will survive for the next three years

98
07:16.165 --> 07:18.083
but revenue will be cut by one-third.

99
07:18.751 --> 07:19.752
All right.

100
07:20.002 --> 07:23.380
So as Head Brand Manager

101
07:23.881 --> 07:26.800
you'd have a six-figure salary of at least 100,000 dollars.

102
07:27.259 --> 07:28.260
How's that?

103
07:28.677 --> 07:30.220
Is that enough to start thinking about it?

104
07:51.658 --> 07:52.659
Jeez.

105
07:57.831 --> 07:58.957
What's the reason?

106
07:59.708 --> 08:01.085
Do I have to tell you that?

107
08:01.502 --> 08:04.171
CGM is the best brand controller in North America.

108
08:04.630 --> 08:06.882
Hongsung is a corner store compared to them.

109
08:06.965 --> 08:08.550
If you stay there

110
08:08.634 --> 08:10.636
all you'll get is early retirement.

111
08:10.719 --> 08:11.720
So why?

112
08:15.265 --> 08:17.017
When making a decision

113
08:17.851 --> 08:20.521
one should be most cautious about money.

114
08:21.438 --> 08:23.107
My worth remains the same.

115
08:23.524 --> 08:25.025
I should be suspicious if I'm offered more money.

116
08:27.111 --> 08:28.445
Don't you think

117
08:29.113 --> 08:31.240
your current worth is being underestimated?

118
08:31.949 --> 08:35.285
Some people might be getting paid more than they're worth.

119
08:44.878 --> 08:46.255
I understand.

120
08:46.964 --> 08:49.550
But I guarantee

121
08:50.592 --> 08:52.803
you'll regret this moment.

122
08:56.849 --> 08:59.059
You shouldn't be doing this, Mr. Jeong.

123
09:02.604 --> 09:03.689
Do you think

124
09:04.398 --> 09:06.817
you did me a favor or something?

125
09:08.777 --> 09:10.821
I considered it an insult.

126
09:12.614 --> 09:14.324
There's something you got wrong.

127
09:15.534 --> 09:18.662
Do you think Mr. Jeong will be grateful for what you did?

128
09:21.373 --> 09:25.419
Are you saying you want revenge for that insult?

129
09:25.502 --> 09:26.545
No.

130
09:26.879 --> 09:28.630
I'm just doing my job.

131
09:29.089 --> 09:32.509
CGM called to say they were looking for a Korea Branch Manager.

132
09:33.343 --> 09:36.180
Someone from Hongsung or a large enough Korean company

133
09:36.263 --> 09:39.266
who has enough influence as a sole proprietor

134
09:39.349 --> 09:40.893
but lacks the funds.

135
09:41.977 --> 09:44.021
I just happened to align with the terms.

136
09:45.105 --> 09:47.191
Who cares about trivial revenge?

137
09:47.274 --> 09:48.483
It's just work.

138
09:55.449 --> 09:57.201
100 DAYS OF PRAYER FOR SUCCESS ON THE 2027 CSAT

139
10:42.704 --> 10:43.705
Mr. Jang.

140
10:58.345 --> 11:00.597
What kind of team leader surprises their boss

141
11:00.681 --> 11:03.100
on a spiritual retreat during the holiday break?

142
11:03.392 --> 11:04.559
You scared me to death.

143
11:05.686 --> 11:06.687
I'm sorry, sir.

144
11:08.563 --> 11:09.982
Anyway, how did you find me?

145
11:10.565 --> 11:13.110
You weren't answering any of my calls

146
11:13.193 --> 11:14.319
so I called your house.

147
11:16.613 --> 11:17.614
Well done.

148
11:19.908 --> 11:21.952
So is there something wrong?

149
11:22.911 --> 11:23.912
By any chance

150
11:25.163 --> 11:27.499
have you heard any news about Mr. Jeong's company?

151
11:29.001 --> 11:30.961
Jeong Seon-hyuk's company? No.

152
11:32.379 --> 11:34.881
CGM acquired his company.

153
11:35.841 --> 11:36.842
CGM?

154
11:37.509 --> 11:39.261
Are you talking about the CGM we know?

155
11:39.344 --> 11:40.721
Yes, they plan to enter Korea.

156
11:41.513 --> 11:43.473
Mr. Jeong is their Korea Branch Manager.

157
11:49.855 --> 11:51.064
Why are you telling me this now?

158
11:52.399 --> 11:54.151
Why didn't you tell me sooner?

159
11:54.651 --> 11:55.736
Come on.

160
11:55.819 --> 11:57.904
You should've started with that.

161
11:58.405 --> 12:00.782
Well, there's a certain flow to conversations...

162
12:00.866 --> 12:02.951
Gosh, what is wrong with you?

163
12:03.035 --> 12:04.619
You're such a strange guy.

164
12:05.329 --> 12:07.831
I mean, don't you know what's important?

165
12:09.166 --> 12:10.250
Jeez.

166
12:16.214 --> 12:18.925
CGM DECLARES KOREA EXPANSION, DOMESTIC COMPANIES ON HIGH ALERT

167
12:30.771 --> 12:32.481
BELOVED BY HOLLYWOOD, OAULD WILL BE LAUNCHED BY CGM

168
12:43.825 --> 12:46.912
WHO WILL SURVIVE THE FASHION MARKET'S GLOBAL BATTLEFIELD?

169
12:53.460 --> 12:57.130
KOREA BRANCH MANAGER JEONG SEON-HYUK

170
13:07.641 --> 13:10.060
CGM'S AMBITIOUS KOREA BRANCH MANAGER JEONG SEON-HYUK

171
13:15.190 --> 13:18.318
Jeong Seon-hyuk must be over the moon.

172
13:19.736 --> 13:21.279
The fact that articles have been published

173
13:21.696 --> 13:25.117
means they've already finished talks with brands and malls.

174
13:27.828 --> 13:29.371
It appears they were

175
13:29.454 --> 13:32.207
strategically laying the groundwork at the three biggest malls.

176
13:32.290 --> 13:33.667
Right as the articles dropped

177
13:33.750 --> 13:35.419
they distributed their entire brand list

178
13:35.836 --> 13:37.754
to shopping complexes and outlets.

179
13:38.505 --> 13:41.091
Did you get the list of brands CGM is launching?

180
13:42.717 --> 13:46.638
There are around 300 global brands, as well as some domestic brands.

181
13:46.721 --> 13:51.518
It basically includes all the brands they control in North America.

182
13:52.561 --> 13:55.397
They've set the table and are telling retailers to eat up.

183
13:56.648 --> 13:58.775
Based on Oauld's entry contract

184
13:59.443 --> 14:01.361
it looks like CGM sacrificed their profit margin.

185
14:02.028 --> 14:03.905
They're essentially trying to eliminate

186
14:03.989 --> 14:05.615
all the domestic brand controllers.

187
14:07.701 --> 14:09.619
If we fight amongst ourselves

188
14:09.703 --> 14:12.914
malls and shopping complexes will have the upper hand.

189
14:13.623 --> 14:15.333
And once the weak are eliminated

190
14:15.417 --> 14:18.503
CGM will monopolize nearly half of the market.

191
14:18.837 --> 14:20.964
Yes, since the early stage of their expansion

192
14:21.047 --> 14:23.300
their intention seems to be full domination.

193
14:29.598 --> 14:33.393
Ma'am, Paradi Mall is requesting an amendment to the Aileye contract.

194
14:34.060 --> 14:36.688
- Aileye just renewed their contract. - Right.

195
14:36.771 --> 14:38.482
If we don't renew the contract

196
14:38.565 --> 14:40.567
they're even willing to pay the penalty.

197
14:41.109 --> 14:43.195
When Paradi Mall first opened

198
14:43.278 --> 14:45.906
they clung onto us and begged us to help them open stores...

199
14:46.698 --> 14:47.699
Didn't they?

200
14:50.368 --> 14:52.704
Since they begged us

201
14:53.205 --> 14:55.332
now they want us to beg them.

202
14:56.541 --> 14:58.126
I doubt they're the only ones.

203
15:00.045 --> 15:01.421
- Mr. Jang. - Yes, ma'am.

204
15:02.088 --> 15:05.175
Gather a list of stores and brands where complications have arisen

205
15:05.258 --> 15:07.010
and give me an initial report by the end of the day.

206
15:07.260 --> 15:08.261
Yes, ma'am.

207
15:08.345 --> 15:09.387
Mr. Gong.

208
15:09.471 --> 15:11.056
Consult with the Legal Team.

209
15:11.640 --> 15:14.851
Compare the size of penalties and sales projections and brief me.

210
15:16.311 --> 15:18.813
You should at least do that to ease your conscience.

211
15:21.441 --> 15:22.484
Yes, ma'am.

212
15:28.198 --> 15:29.199
Goodbye, ma'am.

213
15:30.659 --> 15:32.827
LOIRE OUTLET SCAN-BASED TRADING SALES CONTRACT

214
15:43.755 --> 15:45.549
Hello.

215
15:50.929 --> 15:51.930
Gosh.

216
15:52.931 --> 15:54.391
You should eat a proper meal.

217
15:56.393 --> 15:57.435
What is it?

218
15:57.519 --> 15:58.937
Do you need to report on the penalty scale?

219
15:59.020 --> 16:00.021
Yeah.

220
16:00.105 --> 16:01.398
JIN HAE-JU

221
16:01.481 --> 16:02.524
Go back and wait.

222
16:02.857 --> 16:04.568
I have so many brands to review.

223
16:05.777 --> 16:07.654
Right, then should I go back?

224
16:15.996 --> 16:17.539
You probably didn't eat, either.

225
16:17.622 --> 16:19.165
When you're busy, this is better than a meal.

226
16:25.755 --> 16:27.173
Just go back and wait.

227
16:29.134 --> 16:30.343
This is really good.

228
16:33.680 --> 16:34.973
Let's talk outside.

229
16:35.515 --> 16:37.100
Are you sure? Aren't you busy?

230
16:37.350 --> 16:39.686
If you knew that, you shouldn't have come here.

231
16:42.022 --> 16:43.231
The managing director is inside.

232
16:43.315 --> 16:44.649
- Let's leave. - Okay.

233
16:54.326 --> 16:56.328
The managing director doesn't like you.

234
16:56.411 --> 16:58.538
Says you make problems out of nothing.

235
16:58.872 --> 16:59.998
That's understandable.

236
17:00.081 --> 17:02.292
You change contracts as you please.

237
17:03.126 --> 17:04.377
There's also Mr. Jeong's case.

238
17:04.878 --> 17:05.962
We dealt with him

239
17:06.046 --> 17:08.590
but then you helped him, which led to all of this.

240
17:08.673 --> 17:09.674
You're right.

241
17:09.924 --> 17:12.302
- Gosh, you really... - So

242
17:12.385 --> 17:14.721
when can I get the full amount of penalties?

243
17:15.138 --> 17:17.182
- Approximately. - I don't know, either.

244
17:17.515 --> 17:20.685
There's no guarantee we can get the exact amount listed in contracts.

245
17:20.769 --> 17:22.854
We have to compare the time spent on litigation

246
17:22.937 --> 17:25.273
and the actual amount we can receive.

247
17:26.024 --> 17:27.942
With all of that, when can I get it?

248
17:28.234 --> 17:29.653
- Hey, you... - Hae-ju.

249
17:30.487 --> 17:34.032
I get that it's a struggle, and that you're upset.

250
17:34.991 --> 17:36.618
But we still have to work.

251
17:37.452 --> 17:39.412
I need the timeline so I can prepare.

252
17:40.121 --> 17:41.122
You're really...

253
17:41.206 --> 17:44.334
If every brand under CGM wants to terminate their contract

254
17:44.417 --> 17:46.378
the penalty amount in the contract

255
17:46.461 --> 17:47.712
plus compensation for damages

256
17:48.088 --> 17:49.255
totals 280 billion won.

257
17:50.340 --> 17:52.217
Since it'd be a one-sided termination

258
17:52.300 --> 17:55.095
if we assume it won't go to court and they'll pay up without a fight

259
17:55.178 --> 17:56.471
the amount would be similar.

260
17:57.389 --> 18:00.517
Before the end of the day, at least give me an estimate.

261
18:00.600 --> 18:03.186
I'll report it for now and follow up again later.

262
18:04.562 --> 18:07.065
I'll get it to you by 5 p.m. Happy now?

263
18:08.316 --> 18:09.317
Thank you.

264
18:09.943 --> 18:12.362
But if I were on their legal team

265
18:12.445 --> 18:14.072
even if it's a one-sided termination

266
18:14.155 --> 18:15.824
I wouldn't tell them to pay up without a fight.

267
18:16.282 --> 18:19.119
I'd nitpick and do everything I could to make both parties at fault.

268
18:20.870 --> 18:22.038
Speaking of which...

269
18:23.081 --> 18:25.542
Malls have more than enough power to find a way

270
18:25.625 --> 18:27.585
to make contract termination both parties' fault.

271
18:28.128 --> 18:31.256
So if they agree to pay the penalty without putting up a fight

272
18:31.673 --> 18:33.216
that money is coming from CGM.

273
18:36.720 --> 18:37.846
I'm the one suffering.

274
18:38.388 --> 18:39.389
Mr. Oh.

275
18:40.056 --> 18:41.349
Can we talk for a moment?

276
18:41.641 --> 18:42.767
- Me? - Just a moment.

277
18:47.272 --> 18:48.273
Mr. Oh.

278
18:49.023 --> 18:50.984
Has Mr. Jeong offered you a job?

279
18:51.776 --> 18:52.777
No.

280
18:53.653 --> 18:55.029
Why, did you get an offer?

281
18:55.822 --> 18:56.823
Yes.

282
18:56.906 --> 18:58.408
That bastard...

283
18:59.534 --> 19:00.535
Would you accept if you got one?

284
19:00.827 --> 19:02.620
No, I wouldn't.

285
19:02.704 --> 19:04.873
But I'm annoyed that he didn't even offer.

286
19:04.956 --> 19:05.999
What about you, Ms. Joo?

287
19:06.082 --> 19:07.250
Will you accept?

288
19:07.709 --> 19:09.294
Yes, I'm going to accept it.

289
19:11.546 --> 19:12.547
He told me to bring you.

290
19:13.631 --> 19:14.966
- Me? - Yeah.

291
19:15.425 --> 19:17.469
You see how things are going here.

292
19:17.552 --> 19:18.678
It's hopeless.

293
19:18.762 --> 19:19.971
Let's go together.

294
19:20.054 --> 19:22.515
Do I start right away, then?

295
19:23.057 --> 19:24.142
I can quit right now.

296
19:25.351 --> 19:27.228
Don't quit yet.

297
19:27.812 --> 19:31.483
Why don't you stay here and keep us in the loop?

298
19:35.779 --> 19:36.780
Be a mole?

299
19:48.082 --> 19:50.835
Well, things are hectic for all of us.

300
19:50.919 --> 19:53.129
Did you hear anything from the brand's end?

301
19:54.339 --> 19:56.466
We haven't heard much, either.

302
19:57.008 --> 19:59.260
All right, we'll talk soon. Bye.

303
19:59.719 --> 20:00.887
- Mr. Yang. - Yes?

304
20:00.970 --> 20:03.389
Should I mark Richard Hansen as backing out as well?

305
20:03.473 --> 20:04.808
They do have a monopoly in Asia...

306
20:04.891 --> 20:05.892
- Hang on. - Sure.

307
20:06.476 --> 20:07.644
Hello, Manager.

308
20:10.104 --> 20:11.105
What?

309
20:29.249 --> 20:30.917
This punk's not answering his phone.

310
20:32.335 --> 20:33.336
Hey, Park Gi-tae.

311
20:33.837 --> 20:34.838
Mr. Yang.

312
20:35.463 --> 20:36.798
What are you doing right now?

313
20:37.715 --> 20:39.801
They asked me to move these.

314
20:40.385 --> 20:42.303
Who the fuck did? The buying department?

315
20:47.684 --> 20:48.685
Mr. Yang.

316
20:49.644 --> 20:50.645
Mr. Yang!

317
21:07.245 --> 21:08.496
Where's Mr. Kang?

318
21:10.164 --> 21:11.916
Where is Mr. Kang?

319
21:14.711 --> 21:16.629
Yes, how may I help you?

320
21:17.755 --> 21:19.007
I'm from Hongsung's Sales Division.

321
21:20.216 --> 21:23.261
Did your team tell my staff to haul boxes?

322
21:24.554 --> 21:26.097
He offered to do it.

323
21:26.180 --> 21:27.932
Or did I mishear him?

324
21:28.683 --> 21:31.978
Are you playing games with us over the Aileye contract?

325
21:32.061 --> 21:35.106
Moving a few boxes won't solve the contract issue.

326
21:35.189 --> 21:37.233
What an odd thing to say.

327
21:37.901 --> 21:39.485
- Hey, Park Gi-tae. - Yes.

328
21:39.569 --> 21:41.487
Tell me exactly what happened.

329
21:43.072 --> 21:46.993
Well, Mr. Kang said he'd consider the contract renewal

330
21:47.410 --> 21:49.412
and asked me to help organize the boxes.

331
21:49.871 --> 21:52.081
And that guy over there

332
21:52.332 --> 21:54.834
moved a couple of boxes and then disappeared.

333
21:55.418 --> 21:56.419
Is that true?

334
21:57.712 --> 21:58.713
Well, yes.

335
21:58.796 --> 22:01.007
But I didn't do it on purpose.

336
22:01.090 --> 22:03.176
- I just... - Are you still denying it?

337
22:04.802 --> 22:07.430
Why are you coming at me? I have no power.

338
22:07.680 --> 22:11.601
The contract renewal is the general manager's decision.

339
22:11.684 --> 22:12.685
Exactly.

340
22:12.769 --> 22:13.895
So I'm asking

341
22:13.978 --> 22:16.814
why a powerless bastard like you is fucking around with us!

342
22:16.898 --> 22:17.899
"Fucking around"?

343
22:17.982 --> 22:19.275
You piece of shit.

344
22:19.359 --> 22:21.319
- Hey, come here! - Sir, please...

345
22:21.402 --> 22:22.403
Come at me, motherfucker.

346
22:22.487 --> 22:24.113
Who the hell are you to order me around?

347
22:24.197 --> 22:26.783
Let me go. Do you hear what this punk is saying?

348
22:27.075 --> 22:29.827
That scumbag still thinks he holds the power.

349
22:30.078 --> 22:32.288
Then do you hold the power? Are you CGM?

350
22:32.372 --> 22:34.666
A little shit like you throws your weight around?

351
22:34.749 --> 22:36.250
What a damn lunatic.

352
22:36.334 --> 22:39.337
We were going to spare a few of your stores, but forget it.

353
22:39.587 --> 22:42.048
Get rid of all your stores, you fucking bastard!

354
22:42.131 --> 22:43.841
Who are you to decide that?

355
22:43.925 --> 22:45.635
Don't spare them, you fucking idiot.

356
22:45.718 --> 22:47.136
Damn it, I can't take this.

357
22:47.220 --> 22:48.346
- Let go. - Damn what?

358
22:48.429 --> 22:49.597
I said, let me go!

359
22:49.681 --> 22:51.391
- So what? Try me! - You little...

360
22:51.641 --> 22:53.017
Hit me, you motherfucker!

361
22:53.267 --> 22:54.268
Go ahead!

362
22:54.852 --> 22:56.896
Hey, forget it.

363
22:56.980 --> 22:58.398
Just get out of my sight.

364
22:58.648 --> 23:00.441
I don't care about your business anymore

365
23:00.525 --> 23:01.943
- so get lost! - Hey.

366
23:02.360 --> 23:04.654
I'll leave even if you freaking beg me to stay.

367
23:05.279 --> 23:06.280
Let's go.

368
23:07.490 --> 23:08.700
One more thing.

369
23:08.783 --> 23:10.827
You should call your mother and apologize.

370
23:10.910 --> 23:12.328
Say sorry for being a disappointment.

371
23:12.912 --> 23:13.997
Do you understand?

372
23:14.580 --> 23:17.542
You're nothing but a pathetic fucking loser.

373
23:19.585 --> 23:21.379
What a piece of shit.

374
23:22.797 --> 23:24.549
The power dynamic in this industry always changes.

375
23:24.799 --> 23:26.092
Don't regret it when the time comes.

376
23:26.342 --> 23:27.635
Remember, you started it.

377
23:31.931 --> 23:33.599
Jeez, what an asshole.

378
23:33.683 --> 23:35.268
Gosh, that little...

379
23:37.687 --> 23:41.107
Why would you just do what that punk told you to do?

380
23:41.190 --> 23:42.275
I'm sorry.

381
23:42.358 --> 23:44.318
Moving boxes won't resolve the contract issue.

382
23:44.736 --> 23:45.987
Let's say it actually does.

383
23:46.070 --> 23:47.864
That's even more ridiculous.

384
23:48.906 --> 23:50.783
Will you just keep moving boxes?

385
23:52.827 --> 23:55.580
This wasn't just you moving boxes as an individual.

386
23:55.663 --> 23:57.623
It was Paradi Mall using Hongsung International

387
23:57.707 --> 23:59.250
as their lackeys.

388
23:59.917 --> 24:00.918
Do you get that?

389
24:02.086 --> 24:04.672
I'm sorry, sir. I didn't think that far.

390
24:06.674 --> 24:08.009
You drive, punk.

391
24:08.801 --> 24:10.303
- Yes, sir. - Jeez.

392
24:16.142 --> 24:19.562
Hello, I'm Mo Yu-jin of INA Mall's Sales Team.

393
24:19.645 --> 24:21.272
- Yes, hello. - Hello.

394
24:22.023 --> 24:23.024
Have a seat.

395
24:26.152 --> 24:27.361
Wait, 20%?

396
24:28.154 --> 24:30.990
Yes, as I just told you, 20% for luxury stores

397
24:31.074 --> 24:32.992
and 36% for regular stores.

398
24:33.534 --> 24:35.661
You're raising it by 4% so suddenly?

399
24:36.162 --> 24:37.955
We're not just doing this to Hongsung.

400
24:38.748 --> 24:41.125
Will these margins also apply to CGM?

401
24:42.251 --> 24:43.252
Yes.

402
24:44.712 --> 24:46.756
You're basically telling us to close our stores.

403
24:48.132 --> 24:50.968
Well, if you can't do it, then that's too bad.

404
24:52.428 --> 24:54.430
What if we accept your terms?

405
24:55.014 --> 24:56.557
Will you raise it to 22%?

406
24:57.475 --> 25:00.478
That's very likely if Hongsung and CGM both accept.

407
25:01.229 --> 25:03.231
What will you do if we back out?

408
25:03.689 --> 25:04.732
Will you pay the penalty?

409
25:05.566 --> 25:08.111
Yes, we intend to pay the penalty.

410
25:08.903 --> 25:11.155
The contract renewal is just six months away.

411
25:11.906 --> 25:13.658
But you'd rather pay the penalty?

412
25:15.034 --> 25:17.495
That's what we've decided to do.

413
25:18.788 --> 25:20.706
May I speak to your team leader?

414
25:23.668 --> 25:27.463
They sent me, which is why Hongsung sent you, no?

415
25:28.005 --> 25:29.382
If my team leader came

416
25:29.465 --> 25:31.134
then I'm sure you would have sent yours as well.

417
25:32.135 --> 25:34.512
They want us assistant managers to handle it ourselves.

418
25:34.595 --> 25:35.638
Don't you get that?

419
25:37.765 --> 25:39.142
I have to go now.

420
25:39.225 --> 25:40.601
Let me know when you make a decision.

421
25:40.685 --> 25:43.062
I'll give you until next week.

422
25:43.146 --> 25:44.939
All right, then. Take care.

423
25:52.363 --> 25:53.489
You did well.

424
25:53.573 --> 25:55.116
I would've done the same thing.

425
25:55.199 --> 25:56.868
Oh, not at all.

426
25:57.285 --> 25:58.953
I shouldn't have gone that far.

427
25:59.036 --> 26:00.830
But I was so angry at the moment.

428
26:01.956 --> 26:02.957
I'm sorry, sir.

429
26:03.583 --> 26:05.960
How many times will you apologize?

430
26:06.377 --> 26:07.920
I'm sorry... I mean, sorry...

431
26:08.254 --> 26:09.255
Enough.

432
26:12.425 --> 26:13.843
Over here.

433
26:14.427 --> 26:15.428
The food's still warm.

434
26:15.511 --> 26:16.596
- Hello. - We ordered for you.

435
26:16.679 --> 26:18.556
- Good work today. - Good work, everyone.

436
26:18.639 --> 26:20.141
Good work, you two. Eat up.

437
26:23.352 --> 26:24.562
Nice work, Mr. Yang.

438
26:25.021 --> 26:26.022
What do you mean?

439
26:26.939 --> 26:28.816
Word has already gotten around.

440
26:28.900 --> 26:31.527
Mr. Yang of Hongsung called Mr. Kang of Paradi Mall

441
26:31.611 --> 26:34.238
"a pathetic fucking loser."

442
26:35.698 --> 26:37.200
Is that all they're saying?

443
26:37.283 --> 26:40.369
- Not how I verbally destroyed him? - No.

444
26:40.453 --> 26:43.456
They're just saying you called him a pathetic fucking loser.

445
26:44.790 --> 26:45.833
Damn, that sucks.

446
26:49.003 --> 26:51.839
So are they asking for 20%?

447
26:51.923 --> 26:53.382
Well, yes.

448
26:54.300 --> 26:56.802
I've never heard of anyone asking for 20% in Korea.

449
26:57.094 --> 26:59.055
Did CGM really accept those terms?

450
26:59.138 --> 27:00.473
Will they even make a profit?

451
27:00.556 --> 27:02.725
Exactly, I doubt they will.

452
27:03.434 --> 27:05.019
If anything, they'd lose money.

453
27:05.102 --> 27:07.313
Same with the mall employees. It makes no sense.

454
27:07.396 --> 27:09.232
Contract renewals are in six months.

455
27:09.315 --> 27:11.317
Why would they pay the penalty?

456
27:11.400 --> 27:14.737
They're willing to overextend to increase market power short-term.

457
27:15.279 --> 27:16.364
Why?

458
27:16.614 --> 27:19.116
They could easily beat us even if they took their time.

459
27:22.578 --> 27:24.580
Ji-hye, are you trading crypto or something?

460
27:24.664 --> 27:26.707
Sorry, sir. I just have to send this one thing.

461
27:27.041 --> 27:30.086
- What is it? - Laknes sent next season's designs.

462
27:30.169 --> 27:31.879
I have to share it with Marketing.

463
27:32.296 --> 27:33.422
- I see. - Show us.

464
27:33.506 --> 27:35.049
I understand if it's Laknes.

465
27:35.132 --> 27:37.134
- Should I send it to all of you? - Yes, please do.

466
27:38.928 --> 27:39.929
Okay, I sent it.

467
27:44.684 --> 27:46.060
These designs are intense.

468
27:46.686 --> 27:48.271
I don't get the style these days.

469
27:48.771 --> 27:49.939
Isn't it too out there?

470
27:50.022 --> 27:53.025
The extreme designs sell well in China.

471
27:53.359 --> 27:54.819
That's true.

472
27:54.902 --> 27:57.446
These days, you've got to sell well in China before anything else.

473
28:11.460 --> 28:12.586
- Mr. Gong. - Wait.

474
28:13.879 --> 28:15.506
- Mr. Yang, Mr. Gong! - Mr. Gong.

475
28:16.424 --> 28:17.425
Mr. Yang!

476
28:17.508 --> 28:20.261
NAENGMYEON AND BULGOGI PLATTERS

477
28:22.054 --> 28:23.055
Mr. Yang!

478
28:23.848 --> 28:24.932
Mr. Gong!

479
28:25.016 --> 28:26.350
- Where are they going? - Mr. Gong.

480
28:28.894 --> 28:30.521
Ms. Joo resigned today.

481
28:31.731 --> 28:33.190
Unsurprising, right?

482
28:35.151 --> 28:37.778
Over five people have resigned from Sales Division 1.

483
28:37.862 --> 28:39.989
Team 1's Park Eun-sik also quit.

484
28:40.072 --> 28:41.115
Park Eun-sik?

485
28:42.366 --> 28:44.243
They even took a rookie like him?

486
28:44.327 --> 28:46.954
Well, he claims he's quitting due to a family issue.

487
28:47.580 --> 28:48.914
After what happened last time

488
28:48.998 --> 28:51.667
we did our best to crack down. I can't believe this.

489
28:51.751 --> 28:53.586
Last time was an ethical issue.

490
28:53.669 --> 28:55.171
This time is a bit different.

491
28:56.005 --> 28:58.424
Who can stop them from pursuing better benefits?

492
28:59.008 --> 29:00.009
Even so

493
29:00.343 --> 29:03.554
they should tell us honestly, instead of claiming family issues.

494
29:05.264 --> 29:06.349
All right, that's enough.

495
29:06.432 --> 29:07.892
Let's forget about those who left.

496
29:07.975 --> 29:09.810
Let them go. We have work to do.

497
29:10.519 --> 29:13.981
Any new developments since the last report?

498
29:14.065 --> 29:15.733
Not yet

499
29:15.816 --> 29:17.777
but I have a feeling there will be soon.

500
29:19.487 --> 29:20.488
All right.

501
29:20.571 --> 29:23.824
If any more brands or partners want to terminate contracts

502
29:23.908 --> 29:25.826
don't stop them. Just report it.

503
29:26.702 --> 29:28.537
I'm sure some haven't said anything out of morality.

504
29:28.621 --> 29:29.872
There will definitely be more.

505
29:30.664 --> 29:32.917
And don't be meek when dealing with the malls.

506
29:34.502 --> 29:38.172
But if we don't try to stop them, we'll lose 50% of our brands

507
29:38.255 --> 29:40.174
and 60% of our retailers.

508
29:41.467 --> 29:42.635
Then what should we do?

509
29:43.636 --> 29:45.137
Should we beg them to stay?

510
29:45.846 --> 29:47.431
Won't that just make us look bad?

511
29:48.557 --> 29:50.017
No need to blame them.

512
29:50.810 --> 29:53.854
Ultimately, a company must make a profit.

513
29:53.938 --> 29:57.858
If someone offered me a better deal, I'd take it too.

514
29:57.942 --> 29:59.402
Did you think they were our friends

515
29:59.485 --> 30:01.612
because we always shook hands and ate good meals together?

516
30:02.571 --> 30:03.614
There's no such thing here.

517
30:04.698 --> 30:07.284
The world runs on that kind of hypocrisy.

518
30:07.743 --> 30:08.911
Right now

519
30:08.994 --> 30:11.539
that hypocrisy just feels a bit harsher.

520
30:12.581 --> 30:13.916
It'll be tough for a while

521
30:14.458 --> 30:16.210
but our company won't go under from this.

522
30:16.293 --> 30:17.294
Have confidence.

523
30:18.337 --> 30:19.338
While we're at it

524
30:19.422 --> 30:21.882
take everything we moved to shopping complexes and outlets

525
30:21.966 --> 30:23.300
back to the malls.

526
30:23.384 --> 30:25.136
- Revert them to full price. - Yes, ma'am.

527
30:25.428 --> 30:28.222
Does this mean we're giving up on inventory management?

528
30:28.681 --> 30:30.266
We can't manage the inventory, anyway.

529
30:30.683 --> 30:33.436
At times like this, we should try to get the penalty fees.

530
30:38.899 --> 30:40.651
TEAM 5 LEADER GONG EUN-TAE

531
30:43.737 --> 30:44.989
Yes, what is it?

532
30:51.996 --> 30:53.789
- Hello, Ms. Park. - Hello, ma'am.

533
30:54.790 --> 30:55.916
What is this about?

534
30:56.000 --> 30:57.168
What about CGM?

535
30:58.544 --> 30:59.587
It's China.

536
31:00.004 --> 31:01.422
- Because of tariffs? - Yes.

537
31:01.881 --> 31:05.634
Laknes also entered the Korean market because of tariffs, didn't it?

538
31:06.093 --> 31:09.180
If they deliver to China from Korea, they can avoid tariffs.

539
31:10.139 --> 31:12.099
Look, I get the logic.

540
31:12.183 --> 31:13.851
But it still makes no sense.

541
31:14.185 --> 31:16.228
Why would they go this far?

542
31:17.229 --> 31:19.106
There's a rumor going around Shenzhen.

543
31:19.482 --> 31:20.649
Starting next year

544
31:20.733 --> 31:22.568
new company establishment

545
31:22.651 --> 31:24.820
will be heavily restricted in Shenzhen's tax-free zone

546
31:25.404 --> 31:27.031
That's only three months away.

547
31:27.448 --> 31:30.493
Yes, they must register their company in Korea and China

548
31:30.576 --> 31:31.911
secure distribution centers

549
31:31.994 --> 31:32.995
make initial shipments

550
31:33.078 --> 31:35.206
and generate sales before then.

551
31:35.289 --> 31:38.501
Shenzhen grants tariff exemption only once sales are generated.

552
31:38.584 --> 31:40.044
So once it becomes next year

553
31:40.127 --> 31:42.588
CGM won't be able to receive tariff exemption.

554
31:43.631 --> 31:44.673
Have you verified this?

555
31:45.132 --> 31:47.259
I checked with Shenzhen's Deputy Secretary's assistant.

556
31:47.718 --> 31:50.095
We can win if we drag this out.

557
31:50.888 --> 31:51.889
He's right.

558
31:52.139 --> 31:54.266
If we compete with CGM

559
31:54.350 --> 31:56.769
and pretend to fight while raising the margin rate

560
31:56.852 --> 31:58.479
CGM won't be able to hang on.

561
31:58.854 --> 32:01.357
If they can't enter China's market, there's no need for them

562
32:01.440 --> 32:03.567
to take on such margin rates in Korea.

563
32:06.237 --> 32:08.989
There's another option besides dragging this out.

564
32:09.657 --> 32:11.242
What? You're making me nervous.

565
32:11.784 --> 32:12.785
What is it?

566
32:13.827 --> 32:16.622
Let's start with making back our penalty fees.

567
32:36.517 --> 32:39.186
Why are these punks so confident?

568
32:39.770 --> 32:41.981
No, we understand your position.

569
32:42.064 --> 32:46.569
We can only proceed with CGM. I hope you understand.

570
32:47.027 --> 32:49.280
Then we'll immediately withdraw all of our retailers

571
32:49.363 --> 32:50.489
upon contract termination.

572
32:50.864 --> 32:52.449
I hope you know it'll be very hard

573
32:52.533 --> 32:54.910
to generate this level of revenue in the future.

574
32:56.161 --> 32:57.162
Damn it.

575
32:59.331 --> 33:00.332
Don't mind me.

576
33:02.626 --> 33:03.627
I'll take that.

577
33:03.961 --> 33:05.212
It's okay. Give it to me.

578
33:06.922 --> 33:08.716
What a load of nonsense.

579
33:11.427 --> 33:12.803
Have you made a decision?

580
33:12.886 --> 33:13.887
Yes.

581
33:14.388 --> 33:15.973
We'll clear out all our stores.

582
33:17.016 --> 33:18.017
Sorry?

583
33:18.100 --> 33:20.185
We just can't accept a 4% increase.

584
33:22.062 --> 33:23.439
- But... - As for the penalty fee

585
33:23.522 --> 33:26.108
our legal team will be in touch. Goodbye, then.

586
33:32.114 --> 33:33.115
What was that?

587
33:34.241 --> 33:35.743
After taking care of the penalties

588
33:35.826 --> 33:38.495
Hongsung will enter the Chinese market before CGM.

589
33:38.579 --> 33:40.372
We've already expanded to China.

590
33:40.664 --> 33:42.499
Yes, but our China branch is practically

591
33:42.583 --> 33:44.710
just a distribution channel for Korean brands.

592
33:44.793 --> 33:45.794
So?

593
33:45.878 --> 33:48.047
You suggest we bring foreign brands to China first?

594
33:48.297 --> 33:49.298
Yes, sir.

595
33:49.381 --> 33:52.176
We'll select the ones CGM is most afraid of

596
33:52.259 --> 33:55.346
and Hongsung will plant our flag in China before CGM does.

597
33:56.263 --> 33:57.264
Is that even possible?

598
33:57.806 --> 34:01.226
Would global brands even want to team up with us

599
34:01.560 --> 34:03.562
over CGM?

600
34:04.355 --> 34:06.190
Maybe not if it was between us and CGM.

601
34:08.108 --> 34:09.652
But what about Mantua?

602
34:21.664 --> 34:23.832
CGM may be an industry giant

603
34:23.916 --> 34:25.668
but they can't compare to Mantua.

604
34:25.751 --> 34:28.087
Honestly, if we just look at perfume sales

605
34:28.170 --> 34:30.172
Mantua is in a whole different class.

606
34:30.631 --> 34:33.217
CGM's brands may do well in North America

607
34:33.509 --> 34:36.887
but Mantua has European brands expanding worldwide.

608
34:39.306 --> 34:41.225
They just dump inventory wholesale.

609
34:41.308 --> 34:42.434
Will they consider retail?

610
34:42.518 --> 34:46.021
What if we set everything up in China so they can sell wholesale?

611
34:46.522 --> 34:49.400
It's not like Hongsung is saying we'll be their agency.

612
34:49.483 --> 34:53.195
It's a win-win strategy if they just help us secure brands.

613
34:53.278 --> 34:54.571
There's no reason not to do it.

614
34:54.822 --> 34:59.034
If they do it, Mantua's brands will wholly become ours.

615
34:59.660 --> 35:00.661
He's right.

616
35:00.994 --> 35:03.330
In a fight between CGM and Mantua

617
35:03.997 --> 35:06.458
- no brand would join CGM. - Right.

618
35:06.542 --> 35:08.669
If we can bring Mantua to China

619
35:08.752 --> 35:10.504
we will win.

620
35:10.963 --> 35:14.299
So we'll get the penalties we're owed and win this futile fight too.

621
35:15.342 --> 35:16.343
And those who left us

622
35:16.760 --> 35:19.138
will have no choice but to renew contracts with us.

623
35:19.221 --> 35:21.724
Yes, we can get even better terms.

624
35:26.729 --> 35:27.896
This conversation

625
35:28.188 --> 35:29.690
must stay between us.

626
35:32.109 --> 35:33.110
Park Gi-tae, Lee Ji-hye.

627
35:33.193 --> 35:34.194
- Yes? - Yes?

628
35:34.278 --> 35:35.738
You two should be most careful.

629
35:36.113 --> 35:38.949
People tend to spill when they suddenly get exclusive information.

630
35:39.366 --> 35:40.534
Do you understand?

631
35:41.118 --> 35:42.453
- Yes, ma'am. - Yes, we'll be careful.

632
35:43.787 --> 35:45.414
- Mr. Gong. - Yes?

633
35:45.497 --> 35:48.500
Starting tomorrow, withdraw from all stores requesting new contracts

634
35:48.584 --> 35:49.752
and collect the penalty fees.

635
35:50.627 --> 35:53.213
- Interior construction costs too. - Yes, ma'am.

636
35:53.630 --> 35:54.757
And Mr. Gong.

637
35:54.840 --> 35:57.634
Do whatever it takes to get Sponza on board.

638
35:58.093 --> 35:59.261
That's our lifeline.

639
35:59.636 --> 36:00.679
Yes, ma'am.

640
36:03.015 --> 36:04.141
Let's call it a day.

641
36:11.231 --> 36:12.775
Ms. Park has such an aura.

642
36:13.650 --> 36:15.277
Ms. Park knows my name.

643
36:15.778 --> 36:16.779
Mine too.

644
36:17.237 --> 36:20.365
Hey, Ms. Park knows me better than I know myself.

645
36:20.449 --> 36:22.326
I bet she knows you all better than you know yourselves.

646
36:23.076 --> 36:24.077
Hurry up.

647
36:33.170 --> 36:34.296
All right.

648
36:44.807 --> 36:45.849
Here we are.

649
36:46.391 --> 36:47.643
This dish is

650
36:47.726 --> 36:51.063
roe, caviar, and truffle atop grilled blackthroat seaperch.

651
36:51.855 --> 36:53.524
Wait, I'll set it down for you.

652
36:56.151 --> 36:57.277
Thank you, sir.

653
36:57.736 --> 36:59.029
Eat the roe first.

654
36:59.112 --> 37:00.948
Then the caviar and the truffle.

655
37:01.198 --> 37:02.199
All right.

656
37:07.579 --> 37:08.789
How is it?

657
37:08.872 --> 37:10.123
Wow, it's incredible.

658
37:13.919 --> 37:14.920
Thank you.

659
37:19.550 --> 37:22.511
Hongsung says they'll withdraw all their stores.

660
37:23.762 --> 37:26.223
At this rate, my mall will be full of empty spots.

661
37:26.932 --> 37:29.268
We'll fill those spots with even better terms.

662
37:29.351 --> 37:30.561
Why are you worrying?

663
37:31.270 --> 37:33.188
Change is a scary thing.

664
37:33.856 --> 37:36.024
Even more so when there's no resistance to it.

665
37:37.901 --> 37:38.902
Sir.

666
37:40.696 --> 37:42.406
You have nothing to worry about.

667
37:43.073 --> 37:44.616
Hongsung has no cards to play.

668
37:45.075 --> 37:47.202
That's what makes it weirder.

669
37:47.286 --> 37:50.581
I assumed they'd at least accept 20%.

670
37:52.499 --> 37:55.085
They probably figure contract renewal won't be easy

671
37:55.627 --> 37:57.588
and are trying to get their penalty fees instead.

672
37:58.005 --> 38:00.299
Of course, they'll try to get their penalty fees.

673
38:00.924 --> 38:02.968
But I saw it's not just us.

674
38:03.468 --> 38:05.053
It looks like they're withdrawing

675
38:05.137 --> 38:06.847
from every mall that requested a new contract.

676
38:08.307 --> 38:11.518
This means Hongsung is getting out of the business.

677
38:12.144 --> 38:13.520
They should, if they can't handle it.

678
38:13.896 --> 38:15.022
What else can they do?

679
38:19.067 --> 38:20.694
- Mr. Jeong. - Yes?

680
38:21.194 --> 38:22.487
How long were you at Hongsung?

681
38:23.363 --> 38:24.364
Eleven years.

682
38:25.073 --> 38:26.366
During that time

683
38:26.992 --> 38:28.744
how many crises did Hongsung face?

684
38:30.370 --> 38:31.371
I'm not sure.

685
38:33.206 --> 38:36.418
Hongsung won't fall this easily.

686
38:37.169 --> 38:38.837
I know that better than you.

687
38:42.257 --> 38:43.717
I admire your confidence

688
38:44.176 --> 38:45.677
but don't get too complacent.

689
38:46.595 --> 38:49.640
If things go wrong, we'll be taking a big hit.

690
38:50.307 --> 38:52.017
Yes, sir. I understand.

691
39:02.653 --> 39:03.737
NOAVILLA MALL CONTRACT TERMINATION NOTICE

692
39:03.820 --> 39:05.489
DELMAR MALL CONTRACT TERMINATION NOTICE

693
39:06.990 --> 39:10.410
VICE PRESIDENT KOO IN-MOCK

694
39:14.414 --> 39:15.415
Come in.

695
39:24.508 --> 39:25.509
You wanted to see me, sir?

696
39:30.389 --> 39:31.390
What is all this?

697
39:31.890 --> 39:34.559
We can't resolve this by clinging to them.

698
39:35.394 --> 39:36.770
So you'll withdraw from everything?

699
39:37.896 --> 39:39.773
Do you just want to shut down without a plan?

700
39:40.482 --> 39:42.275
We have a plan, sir.

701
39:42.526 --> 39:43.527
What is it?

702
39:44.820 --> 39:46.029
I'm sorry for asking

703
39:46.113 --> 39:47.948
but may I report to you at a later date?

704
39:51.118 --> 39:53.245
You punk, what do you take me for?

705
39:53.328 --> 39:55.622
Jeong Seon-hyuk offered our Finance Team's leader

706
39:55.706 --> 39:58.667
the CFO position for CGM's Korea Branch.

707
39:59.501 --> 40:02.004
- So? - If I were Jeong Seon-hyuk

708
40:02.087 --> 40:05.257
the first person I would contact would be you, Mr. Koo.

709
40:06.049 --> 40:08.969
Even if he meets with the malls as CEO

710
40:09.052 --> 40:10.929
they'll still talk down to him

711
40:11.013 --> 40:13.640
because he's still the same person, even with CGM backing him.

712
40:14.474 --> 40:17.019
If he wants to talk with the malls on equal footing

713
40:17.561 --> 40:19.604
he needs someone like you, don't you think?

714
40:21.064 --> 40:23.692
So are you keeping it confidential even from me?

715
40:25.277 --> 40:26.319
I'm sorry, sir.

716
41:37.974 --> 41:38.975
Mr. Gong Eun-tae?

717
41:58.203 --> 42:03.125
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

718
42:16.221 --> 42:19.391
TEAM 5 LEADER GONG EUN-TAE

719
42:20.058 --> 42:21.309
Yes, what is it?

720
42:31.778 --> 42:34.739
MY DAUGHTER

721
42:37.576 --> 42:38.994
MOM

722
42:43.999 --> 42:45.584
Hi, Mom. Where are you?

723
42:45.667 --> 42:47.377
Yun-gyeong, are you at home?

724
42:47.460 --> 42:48.503
Where else would I be?

725
42:48.587 --> 42:49.754
You wanted to eat dinner together.

726
42:50.422 --> 42:51.423
Right.

727
42:52.174 --> 42:55.093
But I think I'll be a little late.

728
42:55.719 --> 42:56.720
Unbelievable.

729
42:57.554 --> 43:00.015
I told you I was just going to eat with Min-ji.

730
43:00.432 --> 43:01.433
I'm sorry.

731
43:01.516 --> 43:03.560
I planned to get home early

732
43:03.643 --> 43:04.895
- but something came up... - Whatever.

733
43:05.228 --> 43:06.771
Did I beg you to eat with me?

734
43:07.147 --> 43:08.732
Why make a promise you can't keep?

735
43:08.815 --> 43:10.692
So annoying.

736
43:10.775 --> 43:12.360
And it's my birthday. Seriously?

737
43:12.444 --> 43:15.322
Well, I really was trying to get home early.

738
43:15.864 --> 43:17.199
Whatever, I'm going out.

739
43:17.282 --> 43:18.491
Where?

740
43:18.575 --> 43:20.535
Start eating with Dad. I'll be there soon.

741
43:20.619 --> 43:22.454
Why would I eat with Dad?

742
43:22.537 --> 43:23.538
I'm hanging up.

743
43:40.805 --> 43:43.099
WHEN TURNING LEFT, YIELD TO PEDESTRIANS

744
46:21.049 --> 46:23.009
Subtitles by Eunice Kim
